{"title":"Topicwise Test-18 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Digital circuits-2","fileName":"069_Topicwise Test-18 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Digital circuits-2.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Select the circuit which will produce the given output <em>Q</em> for the input signals <em>X</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>X</em><sub>2</sub> given in the figure</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/95e5a73866bfde72426ff7584d8a78820112ab56.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7573c5ed45b14a1245b23461a3d6248d68fda1c5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/e61e198a6211e529d14e3ce40852c046c2ac8b49.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1fcee59cc1d0b47bbc0d34ce338b12bb65b99c03.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2800930971bb89f5c47d8cec05f2e0be0c4b4875.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b7cb5d37f10997172c196ef7a70404c8c6609c24.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n For a flip-flop with provisions for preset and clear.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Preset and clear operations are performed simultaneously</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> While presetting, clear is disabled.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> While clearing, preset is disabled.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both (b) and (c) are true.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)<br />\n The preset input drives the flip-flop to a set state while the clear input drives it to a reset state. Hence, both are disabled or only one is enabled at a time.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A binary ripple counter is required to count upto 65536<sub>10</sub>. If the clock frequency is 25 MHz, the frequency at the output of MSB ( <em>f</em><sub>MSB</sub> ) and number of flip-flops <em>N</em> required are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 331.325 kHz and 17</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 375.135 kHz and 15</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 381.463 kHz and 17</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 305.256 kHz and 16</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a76b53c516a6374bb9862c96c9de363f1d734dc2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A twisted ring counter consists of 4 flip-flops. Number of used states and duty cycle at the output of the MSB flip-flop are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4 states and 25%</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 8 states and 50%</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n 2<sup>4</sup> states and 100%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 8 states and 12.5%</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b7f14bd873bf933621041fcbec96ce93c891ffe7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The table which shows the necessary levels at <em>J</em> and <em>K</em> inputs to produce every possible flip-flop state transition is called</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Truth table (<em>J</em>-<em>K</em>)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> State transition table (J-K)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Excitation table (<em>J</em>-<em>K</em>)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)<br />\n The excitation table of the flip-flop shows the required excitation to the flip-flop, or the required input to the flip-flop, to go from the given state to the next particular state.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n For a 20-bit counter type A/D converter using a 2.5 MHz clock, the minimum conversion rate is ________ conversions/sec<br />\n (Rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.35","high":"2.43"},"solution":"<p>\n 2.38 (2.35 - 2.43)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/472d20cc044c9ee000b377ff33c20573e6ab1a9d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Given 4-stage ladder DAC using. 15 kΩ and 30 kΩ resistors. For a reference voltage of 5 V, the output voltage for an input of 1011 to the circuit is ______.<br />\n(Rounded off to two decimal places)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/940262df74e040233369ff22c8a14ac573cfa6f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>(Rounded off to two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"10.33","high":"10.33"},"solution":"<p>10.33 (8.25 - 12.36)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/70249c18118372692a11970f9f04c0ef1f613754.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A 5-bit shift register circuit configured for right-shift operation, i.e. Din → A, A → B, B → C, C → D, D → E is shown. If the present state of the shift register is <em>ABCDE</em> = 10110, the number of clock cycles required to reach the state <em>ABCDE</em> = 11111 is _______.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/545316a8cb7d5425401837ad4895547587a5be5c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>\n 4 (4 - 4)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f6877c032a282319da1a4e176461fe17b9498f71.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0a7567993e9be516c0c21060b42f07fead27a112.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the given circuit</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/837d28e84a6be49a4b992af750c4ae50b4f5145e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n In this circuit <img src=\"/media/2886f728f453b4863493e985a1c8b4415b7324aa.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Race around does not occur.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Race around occurs when CLK = 1 and A = B = 1.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2092daf7f6908e2c664a8e414a0eb8690668828b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/90fc2141d2b3dcd31047e88c4788cf30a1caf21e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/09afc0c48d06390b7f2575baec470255abb9d2af.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider given sequence diagram as shown below,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/595a94ddfdbe7adc1c477bc2ed32f5f4d39d00a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>Which of the following logic circuit represents the given sequential circuit?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/092d57f664645a6211b3147ea9ca5239c4ddbf0b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/d68f1b2f5e1d9ca1f5f483d0c60d8eea987bbf69.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/32ea1deaa7537a3297db6f9eaf160545a8ed5466.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/e169fc53de72d9ff9c6bfde0cd06e30629c80b25.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/827938344bcef221a0a3460607ed1700a4684dd1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The a circuit realisation of a combinational logic block as shown in figure to obtain the following truth table involves</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a6bf8c5db729028852083758fe3de1a81464c85c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> NOT and EX-OR gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> NOT and EX-NOR gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> OR and NAND gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Only EX-OR gates.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/6cb7a08245f457ea3048a42f2a6a7187a6dbfd3e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a negative edge triggered <em>J</em>-<em>K</em> flip-flop with inputs <em>J</em> and <em>K</em> as shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c7ca0fe43232a047ca2a4bdb019b1c2f070501ec.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The input to the LED is connected to the <img src=\"/media/b1ee0ac5412e998640d14982cc748fc9a9d86578.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> of the flip-flop (assuming that initially the flip-flop was reset). The duration for which the LED will be ON in the time duration of <em>T</em> sec is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1 sec</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2 sec</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 3 sec</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5 sec</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/6ca98a2b07f0ff959370497dcaf1292207204cfa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Out of the given state diagram of a Moore type sequence detector, which of it represents a “101” sequence detector?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/386c8eaef5485a8d979d3df6d37ee766e65d702c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/38210b2a8e28ee8c8cdde54b205ae834eef2c883.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a84a7bda7066247a0e808a38e8e2a1365cbe15bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b6615a0d095e5e3b88749652b2000a98a7c88d4a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If the initial state (<em>Q</em><sub>2</sub>, <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>Q</em><sub>0</sub>) of the following counter is (000), the modulus of the counter is ________.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/41c8fe0a8ee68e8f764d4f62fba3aea8835842ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"/media/41c8fe0a8ee68e8f764d4f62fba3aea8835842ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"/media/41c8fe0a8ee68e8f764d4f62fba3aea8835842ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"/media/41c8fe0a8ee68e8f764d4f62fba3aea8835842ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" />v</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>\n 2 (2 - 2)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4001382ff5ea959ccbc81d905629154594b61c37.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A dual-slope A/D converter has a resolution of 8-bits. The clock rate is 4.8 kHz. The maximum rate of sample conversion is ______ samples/sec.<br />\n (Rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"9.2","high":"9.6"},"solution":"<p>\n 9.37 (9.20 - 9.60)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c612975373afe85f87f6a8bde15a8754bd85a2bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The exponential F.S. coefficient of output <em>V<sub>o</sub></em> (assume <em>V<sub>CC</sub></em> = 10 V) considering the hold time as <em>T </em>and <img src=\"/media/9b50ddfbabd225800ca037ab8cb83f842384f3b7.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is given by ________.<br />\n Assume the clock ON time to be negligible.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/363bf0d05f3097d31595d628979a8cba54d3309b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0","high":"0"},"solution":"<p>\n 0 (0 - 0)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0ae0ab5eb41f6ce7e7885e1955ddaca682f1bd8f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The digital logic shown in the figure satisfies the given state diagram when <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> is connected to input A of the X-NOR gate</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/aad933a6a0d8ea2d76e36e13d1f22d7af1527f1b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Suppose the XNOR gate is replaced by an XOR gate. Which one of the following options preserve the state diagram?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Input <em>A</em> is connected to <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> .</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ce91b588c5ab08088516f940dbe58967e9202b54.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/408e345bb9e443de03065a9372392ede302201bb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n Input <em>A</em> is connected to <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> and S is complemented.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/242cc3cd6afc42a3eea6b9f76e4272af009b78a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:15.877Z"}